==Strategy==
This stage brings back everyone's favourite midranger, R.Ost, now at 300%, supported with extremely dangerous peons like Star Peng, J.J Jackrabbit, General GreGory, and a Cli-One in the back to snipe your units. And don't forget the second R.Ost that spawns later in the level!
While R.Ost can usually be controlled with strong meatshielding options, like [[Haniwa Cat]] or a very high levelled [[Eraser Cat]], the peons, most notably J.J Jackrabbit, can disrupt this formation. To compensate, use Star Peng and GreGory as a stepping stone to land Jelly Dumpling hits, as well as [[Awakened Doron]] to deal heavy damage to everyone on the field. [[Hitman Cat]] is invaluable here to take out R.Ost's health here, while Talented [[Awakened Bahamut Cat]] can get huge damage off both the peons as well as R.Ost himself. If your units are high levelled enough, try to rush down Cli-One with your units and [[Fishman Cat]] and destroy the base before the second R.Ost spawns. Otherwise, rinse and repeat the same thing you did with the first R.Ost and try not to lose too much ground, lest Cli-One start sniping your base.

===Recommended Ubers===
Due to this Colosseum's Rule, any Uber Rare Cats mentioned will be twice as effective.

*R.Ost Killers: Examples include [[Oni Battlepod Kozuchimaru]], [[Trixi the Merc (Uber Rare Cat)|Trixi the Revenant]], and EPICFEST units like [[Valiant D'arktanyan]].
*Generalists: Examples include [[Shishilan Pasalan]], [[God-Emperor Megidora]], [[Immortal Masamune]], [[Supernova Cosmo]], and most other Ultra Talented Ubers. Thanks to the Colosseum Rule, these units have their damage doubled, allowing them to tear through R.Ost much quicker.

